; DDRAW.dll as the DirectX 5 SDK's ddraw.lib knew it, which the game was
; linked with (src/data/guids.cpp has that SDK's ids). The toolchain's
; DDRAW.LIB is DirectX 3's, and its hint for DirectDrawCreate (the index of
; the name in the DLL's sorted export table) is 6; the original's import
; table has 5. LIB numbers the hints in the order of the sorted names, so
; five names come before DirectDrawCreate here: the toolchain library's
; first six but DSoundHelp. Which one DirectX 5's lacked does not show in the
; exe, only how many there were. Each name is spelled as its __stdcall symbol
; is; tools/place.py builds the import library from this file and the import
; tables from that.
LIBRARY DDRAW
EXPORTS
    AcquireDDThreadLock@0
    DDHAL32_VidMemAlloc@16
    DDHAL32_VidMemFree@12
    DDInternalLock@8
    DDInternalUnlock@4
    DirectDrawCreate@12
    DirectDrawCreateClipper@12
    DirectDrawEnumerateA@8
    DirectDrawEnumerateW@8
    DllCanUnloadNow@0
    DllGetClassObject@12
